---
import Obj from './Obj.astro';
---
<div class="tn-wrap"><section class="tn-band tn-scene" id="tada" aria-labelledby="tada-h"><div class="tn-band__objs tn-hide-sm" aria-hidden="true"><div style="right:5%;top:6%;width:96px"><Obj name="moon" w="100%" class="tn-float slow" /></div><div style="right:20%;top:9%;width:120px;opacity:.9"><Obj name="cloud" w="100%" class="tn-float late" /></div></div><div style="position:relative;z-index:1;display:grid;gap:12px"><h2 class="tn-h2" id="tada-h" tabindex="-1">For grown-ups: the TADA way</h2><p class="tn-lead">You talk with your child. The child tells the story and makes the choice.</p></div><ol class="tn-tada"><li class="tn-tada-step tn-reveal"><span class="tn-tada-step__letter" aria-hidden="true">T</span><h3 class="tn-h3">Talk</h3><p class="tn-tada-step__who">Child</p><p class="tn-p">Your child says what they see. You wait, then add one or two words.</p></li><li class="tn-tada-step tn-reveal"><span class="tn-tada-step__letter" aria-hidden="true">A</span><h3 class="tn-h3">Ask</h3><p class="tn-tada-step__who">Grown-up</p><p class="tn-p">One easy question. Then: “What could they do now?”</p></li><li class="tn-tada-step tn-reveal tn-tada-step--key"><span class="tn-tada-step__letter" aria-hidden="true">D</span><h3 class="tn-h3">Decide</h3><p class="tn-tada-step__who">Child</p><p class="tn-p">Your child picks what happens next and says why. No wrong answer.</p></li><li class="tn-tada-step tn-reveal"><span class="tn-tada-step__letter" aria-hidden="true">A</span><h3 class="tn-h3">Act</h3><p class="tn-tada-step__who">Together</p><p class="tn-p">“What would you do?” Try it once in real life.</p></li></ol><div class="tn-tada-foot"><a class="tn-link tn-link--solo" href="/tada">Read the TADA way</a></div></section></div>
